* SEEDVEH - LAB DATA PREPARATION for the Adabas VEHICLES file (DBID 1, file 12).
*
* This is NOT part of the migration. It manufactures, inside Adabas, the two
* legacy-data shapes the migration has to cope with. Run by
* scripts\seed-source.ps1 (which adds the BA/BB fields first), and re-runnable:
* every pass below is idempotent.
*
*   1. VIN (field BA) for every vehicle - 17 characters, derived from MAKE + ISN
*      so it is stable across runs.
*
*   2. The multi-plate workaround. The old system has no place to record a second
*      registration plate for one vehicle, so operators registered the vehicle
*      AGAIN with the same VIN plus a trailing digit ('...0000011', '...0000012')
*      and A DIFFERENT PLATE NUMBER in REG-NUM. That plate is a real, unrelated
*      registration - not the first plate with a suffix - because registering
*      another plate is the entire point of the workaround.
*      Fourteen vehicles get 1-5 extra rows each. Six of them end up with MORE
*      than three plates, which the new model (max 3) must reject rather than
*      silently drop, so MIGRATION_REJECT gets a decent population.
*
*   3. VEH-TYPE (field BB) - a house-grown type code ('SEDAN', 'LORRY', 'MBIKE'
*      ...) cycled over the file, plus 'X-OLD' every 100th record: a code that is
*      NOT in the mapping table, so the unmapped path gets exercised too.
*
*   4. The POWERTRAIN puzzle - two partial sources, on purpose:
*      (a) the VIN, but only for FORD and BMW, and each in a DIFFERENT position
*          with a DIFFERENT alphabet. That is what real VINs are like: positions
*          4-8 are the manufacturer's own descriptor and nothing standardises
*          them, which is why decoding needs a rule table rather than a formula.
*            FORD  VIN position 5 : E=electric P=plug-in H=hybrid G=petrol
*            BMW   VIN position 8 : I=electric X=plug-in A=hybrid B=petrol
*          Every other make encodes NOTHING - the majority of the file.
*      (b) FUEL-DESC (field BC), 30 years of free text: 'PETROL', 'petrol',
*          'BENZIN', 'ELEC.', 'PLUG-IN HYBRID', 'N/A', blank. Cycled over ALL
*          vehicles, so it sometimes CONTRADICTS the VIN - which the mapping has
*          to notice rather than average out.
*
* Headless run: NO terminal WRITE statements (avoids the MORE prompt).
DEFINE DATA LOCAL
1 V VIEW OF VEHICLES
  2 REG-NUM
  2 PERSONNEL-ID
  2 MAKE
  2 MODEL
  2 COLOR
  2 YEAR
  2 VIN
  2 VEH-TYPE
  2 FUEL-DESC
1 #ISN (N10)
1 #DEL (N8)
1 #UPD (N8)
1 #ADD (N8)
1 #HOLD (I4)
1 #CYC (I2)
1 #CYC100 (I4)
1 #I (I2)
1 #J (I2)
1 #SUF (A1)
* VIN laid out by position: 3 WMI + 6 VDS + 8 serial = 17, then the suffix the
* legacy workaround appends. The redefine is what makes "base VIN vs suffix"
* explicit here and in the extract.
1 #VIN (A25)
1 REDEFINE #VIN
  2 #VIN-WMI (A3)
  2 #VIN-VDS (A6)
  2 #VIN-SER (A8)
  2 #VIN-SUF (A8)
1 #MAKE (A20)
1 REDEFINE #MAKE
  2 #MAKE3 (A3)
  2 #MAKE-REST (A17)
* The VDS, addressed character by character so "FORD puts it in VIN position 5,
* BMW in position 8" can be written as exactly that. #VDS1 is VIN position 4.
1 #VDS (A6)
1 REDEFINE #VDS
  2 #VDS1 (A1)
  2 #VDS2 (A1)
  2 #VDS3 (A1)
  2 #VDS4 (A1)
  2 #VDS5 (A1)
  2 #VDS6 (A1)
1 #CYCPT (I2)
1 #CYCFD (I2)
1 #PTCHF (A1/1:4)
1 #PTCHB (A1/1:4)
1 #FUELD (A20/1:16)
1 #BASE-VIN (A25)
1 #PLATE (A15)
* Extra plates are issued from a range the demo data does not use: every real
* 8-digit plate in the file sits in the 30-31 million band, so 9xxxxxxx cannot
* collide - which matters because REG-NUM is a UNIQUE descriptor and a clash
* would fail the STORE.
1 #PLATENO (N8)
1 #TYPES (A8/1:9)
1 #BASE-ISN (N10/1:14)
1 #EXTRAS (I2/1:14)
1 #LINE (A) DYNAMIC
END-DEFINE
*
DEFINE WORK FILE 7 '/tmp/seed_counts.txt' TYPE 'ASCII'
*
* Custom type codes as the legacy application spelled them. Assigned in code
* rather than INIT <...> so the list stays readable next to the mapping table
* in oracle-init/02_lookups.sql - change these two together.
#TYPES(1) := 'SEDAN'
#TYPES(2) := 'ESTATE'
#TYPES(3) := 'HATCH'
#TYPES(4) := 'COUPE'
#TYPES(5) := 'PICKUP'
#TYPES(6) := 'VAN-C'
#TYPES(7) := 'LORRY'
#TYPES(8) := 'MBIKE'
#TYPES(9) := 'MINIBUS'
*
* The two manufacturers that encode the powertrain in the VIN - deliberately
* using different letters for the same thing, because real ones do.
#PTCHF(1) := 'E'    #PTCHB(1) := 'I'
#PTCHF(2) := 'P'    #PTCHB(2) := 'X'
#PTCHF(3) := 'H'    #PTCHB(3) := 'A'
#PTCHF(4) := 'G'    #PTCHB(4) := 'B'
*
* FUEL-DESC as three decades of clerks actually typed it. Every one of these
* has to normalise to EV / PHEV / HEV / PETROL - or to nothing at all.
#FUELD(1)  := 'PETROL'
#FUELD(2)  := 'petrol'
#FUELD(3)  := 'GASOLINE'
#FUELD(4)  := 'BENZIN'
#FUELD(5)  := 'ELECTRIC'
#FUELD(6)  := 'ELEC.'
#FUELD(7)  := 'EV'
#FUELD(8)  := 'BATTERY ONLY'
#FUELD(9)  := 'HYBRID'
#FUELD(10) := 'HYB'
#FUELD(11) := 'HEV SELF CHG'
#FUELD(12) := 'PLUG-IN HYBRID'
#FUELD(13) := 'PHEV'
#FUELD(14) := 'PLUGIN HYB'
#FUELD(15) := ' '
#FUELD(16) := 'N/A'
*
* Which vehicles carry extra plates, and how many EXTRA rows each gets.
* Anything over 2 extras means more than 3 plates in total - one more than the
* new model allows - so those surplus rows land in MIGRATION_REJECT. Six of the
* fourteen are over the limit, by 1, 2 or 3 plates.
*                     extras   plates   rejected
#BASE-ISN(1)  := 1    #EXTRAS(1)  := 2   /*  3    -
#BASE-ISN(2)  := 2    #EXTRAS(2)  := 1   /*  2    -
#BASE-ISN(3)  := 3    #EXTRAS(3)  := 3   /*  4    1
#BASE-ISN(4)  := 4    #EXTRAS(4)  := 1   /*  2    -
#BASE-ISN(5)  := 5    #EXTRAS(5)  := 2   /*  3    -
#BASE-ISN(6)  := 6    #EXTRAS(6)  := 4   /*  5    2
#BASE-ISN(7)  := 7    #EXTRAS(7)  := 3   /*  4    1
#BASE-ISN(8)  := 8    #EXTRAS(8)  := 2   /*  3    -
#BASE-ISN(9)  := 9    #EXTRAS(9)  := 5   /*  6    3
#BASE-ISN(10) := 10   #EXTRAS(10) := 1   /*  2    -
#BASE-ISN(11) := 11   #EXTRAS(11) := 3   /*  4    1
#BASE-ISN(12) := 12   #EXTRAS(12) := 2   /*  3    -
#BASE-ISN(13) := 13   #EXTRAS(13) := 4   /*  5    2
#BASE-ISN(14) := 14   #EXTRAS(14) := 1   /*  2    -
*                             34 extra rows, 10 plates rejected
#PLATENO := 90000000
*
* ---- pass 1: drop the rows a previous run stored ------------------------
* Identified by the suffix, which only the workaround rows carry. Doing this
* first is what makes the whole program re-runnable.
READ V BY ISN
  MOVE V.VIN TO #VIN
  IF #VIN-SUF NE ' '
    DELETE
    ADD 1 TO #DEL
    ADD 1 TO #HOLD
    IF #HOLD > 50
      END TRANSACTION
      RESET #HOLD
    END-IF
  END-IF
END-READ
END TRANSACTION
RESET #HOLD
*
* ---- pass 2: VIN + VEH-TYPE for every remaining record ------------------
RESET #CYC #CYC100
READ V BY ISN
  #ISN := *ISN
  RESET #VIN #MAKE
  #MAKE := V.MAKE
  #VIN-WMI := #MAKE3
* a make shorter than 3 characters would leave blanks inside the VIN
  EXAMINE #VIN-WMI FOR ' ' REPLACE WITH 'Z'
* the descriptor: filler for most makes, a powertrain letter for two of them
  #VDS := 'ZZ1JZW'
  ADD 1 TO #CYCPT
  IF #CYCPT > 4
    #CYCPT := 1
  END-IF
  IF #VIN-WMI = 'FOR'
    #VDS2 := #PTCHF(#CYCPT)
  END-IF
  IF #VIN-WMI = 'BMW'
    #VDS5 := #PTCHB(#CYCPT)
  END-IF
  #VIN-VDS := #VDS
  MOVE EDITED #ISN (EM=99999999) TO #VIN-SER
  V.VIN := #VIN
*
  ADD 1 TO #CYCFD
  IF #CYCFD > 16
    #CYCFD := 1
  END-IF
  V.FUEL-DESC := #FUELD(#CYCFD)
  ADD 1 TO #CYC
  IF #CYC > 9
    #CYC := 1
  END-IF
  V.VEH-TYPE := #TYPES(#CYC)
  ADD 1 TO #CYC100
  IF #CYC100 > 100
    #CYC100 := 1
  END-IF
  IF #CYC100 = 100
    V.VEH-TYPE := 'X-OLD'
  END-IF
  UPDATE
  ADD 1 TO #UPD
  ADD 1 TO #HOLD
  IF #HOLD > 50
    END TRANSACTION
    RESET #HOLD
  END-IF
END-READ
END TRANSACTION
RESET #HOLD
*
* ---- pass 3: the multi-plate workaround --------------------------------
* A copy of the base record with the VIN suffixed and a different plate.
* PERSONNEL-ID is copied unchanged, which keeps the file's referential
* integrity constraint against file 9 satisfied.
FOR #I = 1 TO 14
  GET V #BASE-ISN(#I)
  #BASE-VIN := V.VIN
  FOR #J = 1 TO #EXTRAS(#I)
    MOVE EDITED #J (EM=9) TO #SUF
    MOVE #BASE-VIN TO #VIN
    #VIN-SUF := #SUF
    V.VIN := #VIN
* A genuinely different registration number - NOT the base plate with a suffix.
* The whole reason the workaround exists is that a second, unrelated plate had
* to be recorded and the file has room for only one.
    ADD 1 TO #PLATENO
    MOVE EDITED #PLATENO (EM=99999999) TO #PLATE
    V.REG-NUM := #PLATE
    STORE V
    ADD 1 TO #ADD
  END-FOR
END-FOR
END TRANSACTION
*
COMPRESS 'deleted:' #DEL INTO #LINE LEAVING NO SPACE
WRITE WORK FILE 7 VARIABLE #LINE
COMPRESS 'updated:' #UPD INTO #LINE LEAVING NO SPACE
WRITE WORK FILE 7 VARIABLE #LINE
COMPRESS 'stored:' #ADD INTO #LINE LEAVING NO SPACE
WRITE WORK FILE 7 VARIABLE #LINE
CLOSE WORK FILE 7
*
END
